  "body": "Title: Nested multicall resets payment guard, breaking batches that mix oracle updates and actions  \nSeverity: Medium  \nTarget: src/Covenant.sol – multicall(), _checkPayment()\n\n## Summary\nThe `Covenant.multicall` helper only tracks “batch mode” with a boolean `_isMulticall`. If any payload within the batch calls `multicall` again (nested multicall), the inner frame sets `_isMulticall` back to `false` before the outer loop finishes. Subsequent outer payloads then hit `_checkPayment` with `_isMulticall == false`, so the contract enforces `msg.value == msgValue` despite still being inside the outer batch. Any sequence that spends ETH on an inner oracle update (non-zero `msgValue`) and follows up with a zero-value call will revert with `Errors.E_IncorrectPayment`, breaking otherwise valid batched flows.\n\n## Impact\n- **Liveness/DoS on self:** Integrators composing helper contracts that themselves call `multicall` can no longer combine price updates and mint/swap/redemption actions in a single top-level batch if the inner helper consumes ETH. The revert occurs even when the batched operations are solvent and previously worked in single-level multicalls.\n- **Composability break:** This undermines the reasons to expose `multicall`—operators cannot safely reuse library helpers that themselves rely on batching, forcing duplicate logic or separate transactions.\n- **User-facing regression:** The revert arises solely from call ordering, not from balance insolvency, producing unexpected `E_IncorrectPayment` errors for otherwise valid flows.\n\n## Root Cause\n- `multicall` toggles `_isMulticall` from `false → true → false` without tracking depth ([src/Covenant.sol#L506-L521](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/main/src/Covenant.sol#L506-L521)). An inner call resets the flag before the outer loop completes.\n- `_checkPayment` (invoked by mint/redeem/swap/updateState) requires exact `msg.value == msgValue` whenever `_isMulticall == false` ([src/Covenant.sol#L556-L560](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-covenant/blob/main/src/Covenant.sol#L556-L560)). After the inner call returns, the flag is false, so the next outer payload reverts.\n- No guard disallows nesting nor compensates for it.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n1. add the following test:\n   ```solidity\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\n   pragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\n   import \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\n   import {Covenant, MarketId, MarketParams} from \"../../src/Covenant.sol\";\n   import {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\";\n   import {MockOracle} from \"../mocks/MockOracle.sol\";\n   import {MockERC20} from \"../mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\n   import {LatentSwapLib} from \"../../src/periphery/libraries/LatentSwapLib.sol\";\n   import {FixedPoint} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\";\n   import {Errors} from \"../../src/libraries/Errors.sol\";\n   import {MintParams, MarketState} from \"../../src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol\";\n\n   contract MC01_NestedMulticallTest is Test {\n       uint160 constant P_MAX = uint160((1095445 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000000);\n       uint160 constant P_MIN = uint160(FixedPoint.Q192 / P_MAX);\n       uint32 constant DURATION = 30 days;\n       uint8 constant SWAP_FEE = 0;\n       int64 constant LN_RATE_BIAS = 5012540000000000; // WAD\n\n       Covenant covenant;\n       MockOracle oracle;\n       MockERC20 base;\n       MockERC20 quote;\n       address lex;\n       MarketId marketId;\n       MarketParams marketParams;\n\n       function setUp() public {\n           vm.deal(address(this), 1 ether);\n\n           covenant = new Covenant(address(this));\n           oracle = new MockOracle(address(this));\n           base = new MockERC20(address(this), \"BASE\", \"BASE\", 18);\n           quote = new MockERC20(address(this), \"QUOTE\", \"QUOTE\", 18);\n           base.mint(address(this), 1_000e18);\n\n           lex = address(\n               new LatentSwapLEX(\n                   address(this),\n                   address(covenant),\n                   P_MAX,\n                   P_MIN,\n                   LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9500),\n                   LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9999),\n                   LN_RATE_BIAS,\n                   DURATION,\n                   SWAP_FEE\n               )\n           );\n\n           covenant.setEnabledLEX(lex, true);\n           covenant.setEnabledCurator(address(oracle), true);\n\n           MarketParams memory params = MarketParams({\n               baseToken: address(base),\n               quoteToken: address(quote),\n               curator: address(oracle),\n               lex: lex\n           });\n\n           marketId = covenant.createMarket(params, hex\"\");\n           marketParams = params;\n\n           base.approve(address(covenant), type(uint256).max);\n       }\n\n       function test_nestedMulticall_breaksPaymentFlag() public {\n           bytes[] memory inner = new bytes[](1);\n           inner[0] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.updateState,\n               (marketId, marketParams, bytes(\"feed\"), uint256(1))\n           );\n\n           bytes[] memory outer = new bytes[](2);\n           outer[0] = abi.encodeCall(Covenant.multicall, (inner));\n           outer[1] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.mint,\n               (\n                   MintParams({\n                       marketId: marketId,\n                       marketParams: marketParams,\n                       baseAmountIn: 1e18,\n                       to: address(this),\n                       minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       data: hex\"\",\n                       msgValue: 0\n                   })\n               )\n           );\n\n           vm.expectRevert(Errors.E_IncorrectPayment.selector);\n           covenant.multicall{value: 1}(outer);\n       }\n\n       function test_singleLevelMulticall_allowsMixedMsgValues() public {\n           bytes[] memory data = new bytes[](2);\n           data[0] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.updateState,\n               (marketId, marketParams, bytes(\"feed\"), uint256(1))\n           );\n           data[1] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.mint,\n               (\n                   MintParams({\n                       marketId: marketId,\n                       marketParams: marketParams,\n                       baseAmountIn: 1e18,\n                       to: address(this),\n                       minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       data: hex\"\",\n                       msgValue: 0\n                   })\n               )\n           );\n\n           covenant.multicall{value: 1}(data);\n\n           MarketState memory stateAfter = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n           assertEq(stateAfter.baseSupply, 1e18, \"base supply should reflect mint\");\n       }\n   }\n   ```\n2. Execute:\n   ```sh\n   forge test --match-test test_nestedMulticall_breaksPaymentFlag -vv\n   ```\n   The transaction reverts with `Errors.E_IncorrectPayment` because the inner `multicall` resets `_isMulticall`.\n3. For comparison, run:\n   ```sh\n   forge test --match-test test_singleLevelMulticall_allowsMixedMsgValues -vv\n   ```\n   This passes, showing the issue is specific to nested multicalls. The control test is included in the same PoC contract:\n   ```solidity\n       function test_singleLevelMulticall_allowsMixedMsgValues() public {\n           bytes[] memory data = new bytes[](2);\n           data[0] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.updateState,\n               (marketId, marketParams, bytes(\"feed\"), uint256(1))\n           );\n           data[1] = abi.encodeCall(\n               Covenant.mint,\n               (\n                   MintParams({\n                       marketId: marketId,\n                       marketParams: marketParams,\n                       baseAmountIn: 1e18,\n                       to: address(this),\n                       minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n                       data: hex\"\",\n                       msgValue: 0\n                   })\n               )\n           );\n\n           covenant.multicall{value: 1}(data);\n\n           MarketState memory stateAfter = covenant.getMarketState(marketId);\n           assertEq(stateAfter.baseSupply, 1e18, \"base supply should reflect mint\");\n       }\n   ```\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\nImplement depth-aware tracking:\n- Replace the boolean with a counter, e.g. `uint256 private _multicallDepth;`.\n- On entering `multicall`, increment the depth, run the delegatecalls, decrement afterward.\n- Update `_checkPayment` to skip the strict equality when `_multicallDepth > 0`.\n- Only perform the before/after ETH balance assertion when `_multicallDepth == 1` (outermost call).\n\nAlternatively, explicitly disallow nesting by reverting if `_isMulticall` (or depth > 0) at entry. The depth-counter approach preserves composability and aligns with typical multicall semantics.***",
